<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Laconia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lakonia, Lacedaemon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Laconia is a region of the south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, centred on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eurotas">Eurotas</a> valley between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taygetus">Taygetus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parnon">Parnon</a> mountains. In the Mycenaean age it held the kingdom remembered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homer">Homer</a> as that of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelaus">Menelaus</a>, and from the Archaic period it was the territory of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a>. It is now a regional unit with its capital at Sparta.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/laconia.jpg" alt="Laconia" width="320" height="370" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lakonia_municipalities_numbered.svg: Badseed derivative work: Pitichinaccio (talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2010_Dimi_Lakonias_numbered.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
